<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01S7">Definition <span data-tag="01S7">11.3.0.12</span>.</a> Let $U: \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}\rightarrow \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$ be a functor between categories, and let $f: C \rightarrow D$ be a morphism in the category $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$. A <em>cleavage of $U$ over $f$</em> is a function </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \{  \textnormal{Objects of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{D}$} \}  \rightarrow \{  \textnormal{Morphisms of $\operatorname{\mathcal{E}}$} \}  \quad \quad Y \mapsto \widetilde{f}_{Y} \]
</div>
<p> which associates to each object $Y \in \operatorname{\mathcal{E}}_{D}$ a locally $U$-cartesian morphism $\widetilde{f}_{Y}: X \rightarrow Y$ satisfying $U( \widetilde{f}_ Y) = f$. </p>
<p>A <em>cleavage of $U$</em> consists of a choice, for each morphism $f$ of $\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}$, of a cleavage of $U$ over $f$. We will denote a cleavage of $U$ by $(f,Y) \mapsto \widetilde{f}_{Y}$. </p>
</article>
